# A block whose query fails at the document root. The `<< >>` below is written on the clause inside the
# block, which a block whose query resolved to nothing never runs, and a block report carries no
# `custom_message` on any of its four constructors -- so the section prints the evaluator's account alone
# and no spelling of this rule would change that. `Parameters` is absent, so the block's query resolves to
# nothing and the value it traversed to is the document, whose path is empty. The reporter had no bucket for
# a finding with no path, and the collector for blocks required `unresolved` absent: exit 19 saying nothing.
rule parameters_are_constrained {
    Parameters {
        Env exists  << Every template must constrain Env >>
    }
}
